1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,800
We were going to talk over together this evening what is meditation.

2
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:34,000
But before we go into that,

3
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:40,560
which is really quite a complex and intricate problem,

4
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:49,400
we ought to be, it seems to me, very clear

5
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:53,720
what it is we are after.

6
00:00:53,720 --> 00:01:00,480
We are always seeking something,

7
00:01:01,480 --> 00:01:10,480
especially those who are religiously minded,

8
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:14,200
and even the scientists,

9
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:20,320
seeking has become quite an issue, seeking.

10
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:23,640
What are we seeking?

11
00:01:23,720 --> 00:01:33,560
I think this must be very clearly and definitely understood

12
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:38,360
before we go into this,

13
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:43,160
into what is meditation

14
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:49,000
and why one should meditate at all.

15
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:59,000
And what is the use of meditation?

16
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,880
Why does it get you?

17
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:07,960
Before we go into that,

18
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:12,880
we must be clear what it is that we are seeking,

19
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:16,120
each one of us.

20
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:26,640
And the word search, seek, run after, search out,

21
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:29,960
implies, doesn't it,

22
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:36,600
that we already know more or less what we are after.

23
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:44,760
When we say we are seeking truth,

24
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:49,560
or we are seeking God if you are religiously minded,

25
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:56,600
or we are seeking a perfect life, and so on,

26
00:02:56,600 --> 00:03:03,400
we must already have in our mind a pattern,

27
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:11,000
or an image, or an idea of what it is.

28
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:18,360
And to find it after seeking it,

29
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:22,440
one must already know its contours,

30
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:26,920
its colour, its substance.

31
00:03:26,920 --> 00:03:31,000
So in seeking,

32
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:38,360
is there not implied in that word

33
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:43,480
that we have lost something and we are going to find it?

34
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:48,760
And when we find it, we shall be able to recognise it.

35
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:55,320
Which means you have already known it.

36
00:03:55,320 --> 00:04:00,760
All that you have to do is to go after, search out.

37
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:07,640
And so,

38
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:13,320
the first thing to realise is not to seek,

39
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:24,600
because what you seek is predetermined, what you wish.

40
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:27,240
If you are unhappy, lonely,

41
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:34,600
in despair you will search out hope, companionship,

42
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:40,440
something that will sustain you, and you will find it inevitably.

43
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:49,320
So, in meditation,

44
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:56,920
every form of search must come to an end.

45
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:12,440
And, as we said when we last met here,

46
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:17,480
that one must lay the foundation,

47
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:26,200
the foundation of order, which is righteousness,

48
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:29,880
not respectability.

49
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:37,480
The social morality is no morality at all.

50
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:45,480
But the morality, order, virtue,

51
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:50,120
that comes out of understanding what is disorder,

52
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:53,240
is quite a different thing.

53
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:58,760
And we said disorder must exist as long as there is conflict,

54
00:05:58,760 --> 00:06:03,080
both outwardly and inwardly.

55
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:12,600
And to bring about order is to understand disorder.

56
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:21,880
And therefore, order is not according to a blueprint,

57
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:26,520
according to some authority,

58
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:31,800
or your own particular experience.

59
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:40,920
And how one brings about, or how does this order come about,

60
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:46,280
must be obviously without effort,

61
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:50,920
because effort distorts.

62
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:54,840
Are we communicating with each other?

63
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:58,520
Because we are talking about something very, very difficult

64
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:02,840
– how to bring about order without control.

65
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:06,920
And that order can only exist

66
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:11,480
when we said we understand disorder, the origin,

67
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:14,120
how disorder comes into being,

68
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:19,240
which is conflict, which is in ourselves, to understand it,

69
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:22,120
not to overcome it, not to throttle it,

70
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:27,640
not to suppress it, but to observe it.

71
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:31,080
And to observe without any distortion, without any choice,

72
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:38,040
without any compulsive, directive impulse,

73
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:43,480
is quite an arduous task.

74
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:50,760
Therefore order, which is virtue,

75
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:56,600
comes about without any effort

76
00:07:56,600 --> 00:08:01,160
when there is the understanding of disorder.

77
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:11,080
And control implies either suppression,

78
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:18,920
or rejection, exclusion,

79
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:23,080
and a division between the controller

80
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:26,920
and the thing to be controlled,

81
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:30,760
and therefore conflict.

82
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:38,200
So if one understands this whole business,

83
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:43,800
control and choice come totally to an end.

84
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:49,480
As we explained, control implies division

85
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:56,200
by the one who controls and the thing that is to be controlled.

86
00:08:56,840 --> 00:09:03,560
And in this division there is conflict, there is distortion.

87
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:07,320
And when you really understand this,

88
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:11,960
that the controller is the controlled,

89
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:19,800
then conflict and control in every form comes to an end,

90
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:25,000
which is the ending of division

91
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:32,040
and therefore comprehension, understanding.

92
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:36,600
When there is understanding of what is,

93
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:40,600
then there is no need for control.

94
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:44,040
Right?

95
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:47,240
So there are these two essential things

96
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:52,200
that must be completely understood

97
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:57,080
if we are to go into the question of what is meditation.

98
00:09:57,880 --> 00:10:05,880
Order with the understanding of what is disorder,

99
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:12,840
and control with all its implications of its duality,

100
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:17,320
contradictory, contradiction.

101
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:23,480
And, as we have explained the other day,

102
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:27,800
the observer is the observed.

103
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:33,400
The one who is angry and tries to get rid of anger

104
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:36,840
is anger himself.

105
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:40,760
And when he divides himself from anger, or from jealousy,

106
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:44,760
or from despair, or from the desire to fulfil,

107
00:10:44,760 --> 00:10:48,120
there must be a contradiction and therefore conflict

108
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:52,360
and therefore distortion. Right?

109
00:10:56,760 --> 00:11:00,360
This is the foundation.

110
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:04,840
And without this, really,

111
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:10,040
you cannot possibly know what meditation is.

112
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:16,040
Don't fool yourself by all the books they write about meditation,

113
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:20,200
all the people that come to tell you how to meditate,

114
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:25,640
or the groups that are formed in order to meditate.

115
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:31,480
Because you see, if there is no virtue,

116
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:37,160
which is order, there must be distortion,

117
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:43,880
the mind must live in contradiction, in effort.

118
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:46,440
And how can such a mind

119
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:53,640
know or be aware of the whole implication of what meditation is?

120
00:11:56,600 --> 00:12:01,240
And, as we said, one must also,

121
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:05,560
not intellectually, with one's whole being,

122
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:09,800
come upon this strange thing called love,

123
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:15,240
and therefore no fear.

124
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:24,280
Without love – you know what we mean by love –

125
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:33,960
love that is not touched by pleasure, by desire, by jealousy,

126
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:38,280
love that knows no competition,

127
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:46,200
that does not divide mind, love and your love.

128
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:51,880
There must be that.

129
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:57,000
All this is necessary.

130
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:05,960
Because then the mind, including the brain,

131
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:14,280
the emotions, or in complete harmony, must be.

132
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:20,600
Otherwise meditation becomes self-hypnosis.

133
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:24,600
Right?

134
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:30,520
You know, sirs, don't go to sleep over this,

135
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:37,160
because as we said, we are communicating with each other,

136
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:41,480
which means we are sharing together,

137
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:45,240
we are journeying together.

138
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:51,400
You are not left behind for someone else to go ahead,

139
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:56,360
either we are going together or not at all.

140
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:03,640
Which means you must have worked during this week

141
00:14:03,640 --> 00:14:10,040
very hard to find out your own activities of the mind,

142
00:14:10,040 --> 00:14:18,040
how it functions, your self-centred activities,

143
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:21,560
the me and the not me.

144
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:25,800
You must have been quite familiar with yourself

145
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:30,280
and all the tricks that the mind plays upon itself,

146
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:32,680
the illusions and the delusions,

147
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:38,040
the image and the imagination that one has.

148
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:45,000
And the romantic ideas,

149
00:14:45,960 --> 00:14:52,760
because a mind that is capable of sentimentality

150
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:56,440
is incapable of love,

151
00:14:56,440 --> 00:15:04,120
because sentiment breeds cruelty, brutality, violence,

152
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:07,240
not love.

153
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:15,480
So if you have, and I hope for your own sake,

154
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:20,200
not because of me, of the speaker,

155
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:27,720
you have more or less deeply established this in yourself.

156
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:45,160
Which is quite an arduous, demanding, tremendous, inward discipline.

157
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:49,480
Discipline being learning.

158
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:54,360
Not learning from another,

159
00:15:54,840 --> 00:16:01,720
but learning by observing what is going on in yourself.

160
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:05,600
And that observation is not possible

161
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:09,880
if there is any form of prejudice, conclusion,

162
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:14,840
a formula according to which you are observing.

163
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:20,120
If you are observing according to some psychologist,

164
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:22,440
you really are not observing yourself,

165
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:25,880
you are observing what the psychologist has said to you,

166
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:29,560
and through that you are observing.

167
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:36,200
Therefore there is no self-knowing.

168
00:16:38,280 --> 00:16:45,960
And this implies an awareness.

169
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:53,320
You know, there are many schools in Asia,

170
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:59,480
and I believe they are creeping into this country too,

171
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:03,160
where you are being taught how to be aware,

172
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:06,440
or how to be attentive.

173
00:17:10,520 --> 00:17:13,400
Now the first thing is, if I may point out,

174
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:16,680
don't join anything.

175
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:23,560
Don't join any group, any organisation.

176
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:32,040
I hope there is nobody here who is the head of organisations,

177
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:38,360
or group leaders.

178
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:41,880
Don't.

179
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:47,640
Because you need a mind

180
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:53,160
that is capable to stand completely alone,

181
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:58,280
not be burdened by the propaganda of others,

182
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:02,680
or the experiences of others.

183
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:08,280
Enlightenment doesn't come through a leader,

184
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:11,240
through a teacher.

185
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:19,080
It comes through understanding of what is,

186
00:18:19,080 --> 00:18:24,280
which is in yourself, not running away from yourself.

187
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:29,560
So don't, if I may most respectfully suggest,

188
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:33,080
don't join anything,

189
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:40,120
especially the religious kind,

190
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:48,200
where they promise you nirvana or God for five dollars,

191
00:18:49,880 --> 00:18:55,560
or give you some kind of talisman,

192
00:18:56,120 --> 00:18:58,840
in the shape of words.

193
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:02,360
We will go into that presently.

194
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Because the mind has to understand

195
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:11,480
actually what is going on in the psychological field,

196
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:13,880
in its own field,

197
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:18,120
therefore it must be aware of what is going on,

198
00:19:18,120 --> 00:19:21,960
aware without any distortion,

199
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:25,800
without any choice, without any resentment,

200
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:30,360
bitterness, explanation, or justification,

201
00:19:30,360 --> 00:19:33,640
just to observe.

202
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:46,440
Now if this is laid happily, easily,

203
00:19:46,440 --> 00:19:50,280
with great joy,

204
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:54,760
not compulsively,

205
00:19:54,760 --> 00:20:00,680
but with ease, with felicity,

206
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:07,000
without any hope of reaching anything.

207
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:11,640
Because if you have hope,

208
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:16,040
you are moving away from despair.

209
00:20:16,040 --> 00:20:19,240
Therefore one has to understand despair,

210
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:23,800
not search out hope.

211
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:31,160
So, despair comes only

212
00:20:31,160 --> 00:20:36,200
when there is no understanding of what is.

213
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:41,880
Out of despair you have bitterness.

214
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:44,440
In the understanding of what is,

215
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:49,320
there is neither despair nor hope.

216
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:58,760
All this is asking too much of the human mind, isn't it?

217
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:10,840
Unless you ask the impossible,

218
00:21:10,840 --> 00:21:16,040
you fall into the trap of what is possible.

219
00:21:16,680 --> 00:21:21,160
And that trap is very easy.

220
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:27,640
One has to ask the utmost of the mind.

221
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:31,960
The mind has to ask, and the heart,

222
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:38,840
at the greatest demand.

223
00:21:39,080 --> 00:21:45,640
Otherwise we will slip into the most easiest

224
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:53,160
– the possible, the convenient, the comfortable.

225
00:21:56,440 --> 00:22:00,120
Are we all together still?

226
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:07,000
Verbally, probably you are,

227
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:11,160
but the word is not the thing.

228
00:22:11,960 --> 00:22:15,560
What we have done is to describe,

229
00:22:15,560 --> 00:22:21,000
the description is not the described.

230
00:22:22,440 --> 00:22:28,120
So if you are taking a journey with the speaker,

231
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:35,560
you are taking the journey actually, not theoretically,

232
00:22:36,600 --> 00:22:40,040
not as an idea,

233
00:22:40,040 --> 00:22:49,080
but something that you yourself are actually observing,

234
00:22:51,480 --> 00:22:56,520
and therefore not experiencing.

235
00:22:57,320 --> 00:23:01,240
There is a difference between observation

236
00:23:01,240 --> 00:23:06,920
and exploration and experience.

237
00:23:07,080 --> 00:23:10,360
May I go on into all this?

238
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:19,480
I don't know how you stand all this!

239
00:23:27,640 --> 00:23:33,240
Because you say this is the life of the speaker,

240
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:38,520
therefore it can go on endlessly,

241
00:23:38,520 --> 00:23:44,680
because there is an everlasting fountain.

242
00:23:45,480 --> 00:23:51,800
But you, the other, the listener,

243
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:59,880
unless you also have travelled deeply, inwardly,

244
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:03,400
it will have very little meaning.

245
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:17,960
So we are asking, what is meditation?

246
00:24:21,080 --> 00:24:26,040
And why we should meditate at all?

247
00:24:26,120 --> 00:24:31,000
Why all this fuss about this word?

248
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:34,760
Probably for some of you, or many of you,

249
00:24:34,760 --> 00:24:39,000
it is the first time you hear that word.

250
00:24:39,880 --> 00:24:44,440
Or you have already a concept of it,

251
00:24:44,440 --> 00:24:50,120
or already you have been told by some wandering monk from India

252
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:56,760
that you should meditate, and gives your formula.

253
00:24:56,760 --> 00:25:03,400
And you, unfortunately, out of your greed,

254
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:10,840
and it is greed and nothing else, follow him.

255
00:25:12,520 --> 00:25:16,920
Here we are not offering you a thing.

256
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:20,440
Please, let's understand that.

257
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:30,440
Because any formula, any method, any system,

258
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:35,400
soon becomes repetitive and mechanical.

259
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:43,880
It doesn't matter who gives that formula, or that system.

260
00:25:44,880 --> 00:25:53,880
If you practise it, you become what the method offers.

261
00:25:53,880 --> 00:25:59,640
And what the method offers is not truth,

262
00:26:01,640 --> 00:26:09,160
because truth is a living thing, method is mechanical.

263
00:26:09,160 --> 00:26:16,120
And if you practise it, in the practice,

264
00:26:16,120 --> 00:26:20,360
watch in yourself, there is the one who practises

265
00:26:20,360 --> 00:26:23,800
and the thing to be practised.

266
00:26:23,800 --> 00:26:27,160
Therefore division, therefore conflict,

267
00:26:27,160 --> 00:26:32,280
therefore distortion, therefore disorder.

268
00:26:33,640 --> 00:26:35,640
Is that clear?

269
00:26:35,640 --> 00:26:43,720
Therefore don't accept any system from anybody.

270
00:26:51,880 --> 00:26:54,680
Yes, sirs.

271
00:26:56,520 --> 00:27:02,920
Which means you have to observe without any support,

272
00:27:02,920 --> 00:27:06,600
without any encouragement.

273
00:27:09,080 --> 00:27:14,600
Observation is entirely different from exploration,

274
00:27:14,600 --> 00:27:18,760
which involves analysis.

275
00:27:20,120 --> 00:27:22,280
Right?

276
00:27:22,280 --> 00:27:26,680
In analysis there is always the analyser

277
00:27:26,680 --> 00:27:30,200
and the thing to be analysed.

278
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:33,080
Exploring.

279
00:27:33,080 --> 00:27:39,640
There must be an entity who explores.

280
00:27:40,200 --> 00:27:47,080
So that is, exploration is different from observation.

281
00:27:47,320 --> 00:27:52,360
Observation is a continuous learning,

282
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:57,480
not continuous accumulation.

283
00:27:57,640 --> 00:28:00,440
I hope you see the difference.

284
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:05,800
Learning is different from learning in order to accumulate,

285
00:28:05,800 --> 00:28:12,680
and from that accumulation act, or think.

286
00:28:16,600 --> 00:28:22,280
Whereas in exploration you are accumulating,

287
00:28:23,280 --> 00:28:28,040
there the mind is acquiring.

288
00:28:30,120 --> 00:28:38,760
And from that acquisition, act, thinks, and so on.

289
00:28:39,960 --> 00:28:49,240
So enquiry may be logical, must be logical,

290
00:28:49,240 --> 00:28:53,000
sane, rational,

291
00:28:53,720 --> 00:28:57,000
but observation is entirely different.

292
00:28:57,000 --> 00:29:00,440
To observe without the observer.

293
00:29:00,440 --> 00:29:02,480
We have gone into it, I won't go into it now

294
00:29:02,480 --> 00:29:05,480
because there won't be time.

295
00:29:05,480 --> 00:29:09,960
Then the whole question of experience.

296
00:29:09,960 --> 00:29:15,480
I wonder why we want experience.

297
00:29:15,480 --> 00:29:21,560
Have you ever thought about it?

298
00:29:21,960 --> 00:29:29,560
We have thousands of experiences all the time,

299
00:29:29,560 --> 00:29:34,120
of which you are cognisant or ignorant.

300
00:29:34,120 --> 00:29:38,760
Experiences are happening.

301
00:29:38,840 --> 00:29:46,120
But we want deeper and wider experiences. Why?

302
00:29:49,480 --> 00:29:54,680
Don't you all want marvellous experiences?

303
00:29:55,160 --> 00:30:05,480
Mystical, mysterious, profound, transcendental, godly, spiritual?

304
00:30:05,480 --> 00:30:10,200
You want them, don't you? Why?

305
00:30:14,680 --> 00:30:20,680
Isn't it because one's own life is so shoddy,

306
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:26,600
so miserable, so small, so petty?

307
00:30:26,600 --> 00:30:29,000
No?

308
00:30:30,040 --> 00:30:33,800
And therefore you want to forget those

309
00:30:33,880 --> 00:30:39,080
and move into another dimension altogether.

310
00:30:40,040 --> 00:30:44,360
How can a petty little mind,

311
00:30:44,360 --> 00:30:48,920
worried, fearful, occupied with the furniture,

312
00:30:48,920 --> 00:30:52,920
with the cook, with the worries, you know,

313
00:30:52,920 --> 00:30:55,640
problem after problem,

314
00:30:55,640 --> 00:30:59,320
how can such a mind

315
00:31:00,280 --> 00:31:02,440
experience anything

316
00:31:02,440 --> 00:31:07,000
than its own projection and activity?

317
00:31:08,920 --> 00:31:14,280
And to demand greater experience

318
00:31:14,840 --> 00:31:19,560
is to escape from what is.

319
00:31:19,880 --> 00:31:22,280
And it is only through what is,

320
00:31:22,280 --> 00:31:26,760
is the most mysterious thing in life.

321
00:31:29,320 --> 00:31:36,360
So, an experience also is involved,

322
00:31:36,360 --> 00:31:39,640
the whole process of recognition,

323
00:31:39,640 --> 00:31:42,760
otherwise you wouldn't know it if you had an experience.

324
00:31:42,760 --> 00:31:46,760
You must recognise it as pleasant, or transcendental,

325
00:31:46,760 --> 00:31:51,320
or noble, or beautiful, happy, this or that.

326
00:31:51,320 --> 00:31:55,320
Otherwise you won't know it is an experience.

327
00:31:55,320 --> 00:32:01,000
So, when you recognise it, it means you have already known.

328
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:05,960
So your experiences generally, vastly,

329
00:32:05,960 --> 00:32:11,320
are out of the past,

330
00:32:11,320 --> 00:32:15,720
therefore there is nothing new in it.

331
00:32:17,640 --> 00:32:23,480
So there is a difference between observation,

332
00:32:23,480 --> 00:32:28,600
seeing, exploring,

333
00:32:28,600 --> 00:32:33,640
critically, rationally, sanely,

334
00:32:33,640 --> 00:32:39,560
and this craving for experience.

335
00:32:41,160 --> 00:32:45,640
Now, if that is clear,

336
00:32:46,200 --> 00:32:49,640
clear not verbally or intellectually,

337
00:32:49,640 --> 00:32:53,400
but clear in the sense that you have put all that aside

338
00:32:53,400 --> 00:32:59,960
completely, including the method,

339
00:32:59,960 --> 00:33:03,640
purpose, search.

340
00:33:06,040 --> 00:33:12,120
You know, all this is extraordinarily subtle,

341
00:33:12,120 --> 00:33:16,920
demands great attention inwardly.

342
00:33:16,920 --> 00:33:24,680
Then we can go and ask, what is meditation?

343
00:33:24,680 --> 00:33:32,040
What is all this noise they make about meditation?

344
00:33:32,920 --> 00:33:37,960
Volumes have been written.

345
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:41,640
There are great – I don't know about great –

346
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:46,680
yogis come and teach you how to meditate.

347
00:33:46,920 --> 00:33:51,000
Now, the first thing to find is,

348
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:54,760
you really don't know anything about it, do you?

349
00:33:54,760 --> 00:33:59,800
Actually, unless you are told. Right?

350
00:33:59,800 --> 00:34:03,400
Do let's be a little bit honest.

351
00:34:05,800 --> 00:34:10,440
But the whole of Asian talks about meditation.

352
00:34:10,440 --> 00:34:14,120
That is one of their habits.

353
00:34:14,200 --> 00:34:19,320
As one of their habits to believe in God or something else.

354
00:34:20,120 --> 00:34:26,120
They sit for ten minutes a day in a quiet room

355
00:34:26,120 --> 00:34:32,360
and meditate, concentrate,

356
00:34:32,360 --> 00:34:36,040
fix their mind on an image.

357
00:34:36,040 --> 00:34:40,040
That image is created by themselves,

358
00:34:40,040 --> 00:34:45,720
or somebody else has offered through propaganda that image.

359
00:34:46,760 --> 00:34:50,680
And during those ten minutes they try to control their mind

360
00:34:50,680 --> 00:34:53,240
and battle with the control,

361
00:34:53,240 --> 00:34:56,360
because the mind wants to go off and battle,

362
00:34:56,360 --> 00:34:57,960
pull it back and forth.

363
00:34:57,960 --> 00:35:02,040
You know, that game they play, everlastingly.

364
00:35:02,040 --> 00:35:05,320
And that is what they call meditation.

365
00:35:05,320 --> 00:35:08,280
Right?

366
00:35:10,040 --> 00:35:15,000
Then what is meditation?

367
00:35:17,560 --> 00:35:20,680
First of all,

368
00:35:22,680 --> 00:35:25,960
the mind,

369
00:35:25,960 --> 00:35:31,160
this mind that chatters,

370
00:35:31,160 --> 00:35:34,200
that projects ideas,

371
00:35:34,200 --> 00:35:36,680
that has contradiction,

372
00:35:36,840 --> 00:35:42,120
that lives in constant conflict, in comparison,

373
00:35:42,120 --> 00:35:49,000
that mind must obviously be very quiet, mustn't it?

374
00:35:49,000 --> 00:35:55,320
To observe, that mind must be extraordinarily quiet.

375
00:35:55,480 --> 00:35:57,560
Right?

376
00:35:57,560 --> 00:36:00,600
If I am to listen to what you are saying,

377
00:36:00,600 --> 00:36:03,720
I must give attention to what you are saying.

378
00:36:03,720 --> 00:36:05,960
I can't be chattering,

379
00:36:05,960 --> 00:36:09,160
I can't be thinking about something else.

380
00:36:09,160 --> 00:36:12,040
I mustn't compare with what you are saying,

381
00:36:12,040 --> 00:36:14,040
with what I already know.

382
00:36:14,040 --> 00:36:20,440
I must actually completely listen to you.

383
00:36:21,400 --> 00:36:26,600
That means the mind must be attentive,

384
00:36:26,600 --> 00:36:33,560
must be silent, must be quiet, mustn't it?

385
00:36:33,560 --> 00:36:36,760
Therefore,

386
00:36:38,360 --> 00:36:42,200
seeing the necessity

387
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:48,360
that to observe clearly, the mind must be quiet.

388
00:36:48,520 --> 00:36:50,200
Right?

389
00:36:50,200 --> 00:36:54,760
To see clearly, the mind must be quiet.

390
00:36:59,240 --> 00:37:02,520
And because

391
00:37:03,800 --> 00:37:10,600
it is imperative to see clearly the whole structure of violence,

392
00:37:10,600 --> 00:37:17,640
and therefore to look at it, the mind must be completely still.

393
00:37:18,360 --> 00:37:20,280
Therefore you have a still mind.

394
00:37:20,280 --> 00:37:22,280
I don't know if you are following this.

395
00:37:22,280 --> 00:37:26,680
You don't have to cultivate a still mind.

396
00:37:26,680 --> 00:37:29,400
Right, sirs?

397
00:37:29,400 --> 00:37:34,920
Because to cultivate a still mind

398
00:37:34,920 --> 00:37:43,000
implies the one who cultivates in the field of time,

399
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:46,680
that which he hopes to achieve.

400
00:37:46,680 --> 00:37:51,880
See all that what I have just now said, see the difficulty.

401
00:37:51,880 --> 00:37:54,440
Right?

402
00:37:54,440 --> 00:38:00,760
Because all the people who try to teach meditation,

403
00:38:00,760 --> 00:38:04,040
they say, control your mind.

404
00:38:04,040 --> 00:38:09,800
Your mind must be absolutely quiet.

405
00:38:10,040 --> 00:38:12,440
And you try to control it,

406
00:38:12,440 --> 00:38:15,640
and so everlastingly battle with it,

407
00:38:15,640 --> 00:38:19,080
and spend forty years controlling it,

408
00:38:19,080 --> 00:38:23,160
which is completely silly,

409
00:38:27,160 --> 00:38:32,200
because any schoolboy can concentrate.

410
00:38:36,680 --> 00:38:39,000
Control.

411
00:38:39,000 --> 00:38:41,000
We are not saying that at all.

412
00:38:41,000 --> 00:38:44,600
We are saying on the contrary.

413
00:38:45,160 --> 00:38:49,480
The mind that observes – please do listen to this –

414
00:38:49,480 --> 00:38:55,640
that observes, doesn't analyse, is not seeking experience,

415
00:38:55,640 --> 00:38:59,080
merely observes,

416
00:39:01,160 --> 00:39:05,320
must be free from all noise.

417
00:39:05,320 --> 00:39:07,880
Right?

418
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:15,800
And therefore the mind becomes completely quiet.

419
00:39:16,920 --> 00:39:21,400
If I am to listen to you, I must listen to you,

420
00:39:21,640 --> 00:39:25,160
not translate what you are saying,

421
00:39:25,160 --> 00:39:29,160
or interpret what you are saying to suit myself,

422
00:39:29,160 --> 00:39:31,720
or to condemn you or to judge you.

423
00:39:31,800 --> 00:39:34,680
Must listen.

424
00:39:34,920 --> 00:39:39,800
So that very act of listening is attention,

425
00:39:39,800 --> 00:39:44,440
which need not be practised at all.

426
00:39:45,480 --> 00:39:51,560
If you practise it, you have already become inattentive.

427
00:39:53,160 --> 00:39:56,280
Are you following all this?

428
00:39:56,280 --> 00:40:02,360
So when you are attentive and your mind orders off,

429
00:40:02,360 --> 00:40:05,000
which indicates it is inattentive,

430
00:40:05,000 --> 00:40:09,480
let it wander off and know that it is inattentive,

431
00:40:09,480 --> 00:40:16,280
and the very awareness of that inattention is attention.

432
00:40:17,880 --> 00:40:22,120
Don't battle with inattention.

433
00:40:23,080 --> 00:40:28,840
Don't try to say, I must be attentive, which is childish.

434
00:40:29,560 --> 00:40:33,080
Know that you are inattentive.

435
00:40:33,880 --> 00:40:38,760
Be aware choicelessly that you are inattentive.

436
00:40:38,760 --> 00:40:41,560
What of it?

437
00:40:44,120 --> 00:40:48,840
But the moment in that inattention there is action,

438
00:40:48,840 --> 00:40:52,360
be aware of that action.

439
00:40:54,280 --> 00:40:59,960
Silence of the mind is the beauty of itself,

440
00:40:59,960 --> 00:41:04,040
is the beauty in itself.

441
00:41:04,840 --> 00:41:11,000
To listen to the bird, to the voice of a human being,

442
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:14,360
to the politician, to the priest,

443
00:41:14,360 --> 00:41:18,600
to all the noise of propaganda that goes on,

444
00:41:18,600 --> 00:41:24,600
to listen completely silently,

445
00:41:26,680 --> 00:41:32,920
and then you hear much more, you see much more.

446
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:42,200
Now, that silence is not possible

447
00:41:42,200 --> 00:41:48,280
if your body, the organism,

448
00:41:49,800 --> 00:41:53,800
is not also completely still.

449
00:41:54,840 --> 00:41:57,720
You understand?

450
00:41:59,560 --> 00:42:06,760
If your body, the organ, with all its nervous responses,

451
00:42:07,320 --> 00:42:10,280
all the fidgeting,

452
00:42:10,280 --> 00:42:14,040
the ceaseless movement of fingers, the eyes,

453
00:42:14,040 --> 00:42:21,080
you know, the restlessness of the body,

454
00:42:21,240 --> 00:42:25,880
that must be completely still.

455
00:42:27,080 --> 00:42:32,600
Have you ever tried sitting completely still,

456
00:42:33,560 --> 00:42:41,880
without a single movement of the body, including the eyes?

457
00:42:42,120 --> 00:42:45,960
Do it sometime and you will see.

458
00:42:48,360 --> 00:42:51,080
You may do it for five minutes or two minutes,

459
00:42:51,080 --> 00:42:53,080
that's good enough.

460
00:42:53,080 --> 00:42:56,600
Don't say, how am I to keep it for ten minutes, for an hour.

461
00:42:56,600 --> 00:43:00,600
Don't. That's greed.

462
00:43:02,760 --> 00:43:06,920
To do it for two minutes is enough.

463
00:43:07,560 --> 00:43:13,880
And in that two minutes the whole of this thing is revealed,

464
00:43:13,880 --> 00:43:17,480
if you know how to look.

465
00:43:19,320 --> 00:43:22,680
So the body must be still,

466
00:43:24,840 --> 00:43:28,680
because then the...

467
00:43:28,680 --> 00:43:37,960
the flow of the blood to the head becomes more.

468
00:43:37,960 --> 00:43:40,680
Right?

469
00:43:43,240 --> 00:43:47,640
If you sit crouched, sloppy,

470
00:43:47,640 --> 00:43:53,240
then it is more difficult for the blood to go to the head.

471
00:43:53,800 --> 00:44:00,600
Which means the body has its own intelligence,

472
00:44:02,760 --> 00:44:09,000
which the mind has spoilt, thought has destroyed.

473
00:44:09,000 --> 00:44:15,560
Thought seeks pleasure,

474
00:44:16,920 --> 00:44:23,000
therefore tasty foods – you follow? – overeating,

475
00:44:23,000 --> 00:44:28,680
indulging, sexually, in all the ways,

476
00:44:29,240 --> 00:44:32,920
compelling the body to do certain things.

477
00:44:32,920 --> 00:44:36,840
If it is lazy, force it not to be lazy,

478
00:44:36,840 --> 00:44:40,520
or take a pill to keep awake.

479
00:44:41,080 --> 00:44:47,960
That way you are destroying the innate intelligence of the organism.

480
00:44:47,960 --> 00:44:57,240
And when you do that, the organism becomes insensitive.

481
00:44:59,320 --> 00:45:04,120
And so you need great sensitivity.

482
00:45:05,640 --> 00:45:09,880
Therefore one has to watch what one eats, all that.

483
00:45:09,880 --> 00:45:14,040
I won't go into all that business, it is up to you.

484
00:45:14,040 --> 00:45:20,120
Because if you overeat, you know what happens,

485
00:45:20,120 --> 00:45:26,120
you know, all the ugliness of all that.

486
00:45:26,920 --> 00:45:32,760
So you need a body that is highly sensitive,

487
00:45:32,760 --> 00:45:36,120
greatly intelligent.

488
00:45:36,120 --> 00:45:46,360
And therefore love,

489
00:45:51,640 --> 00:45:55,720
which doesn't become pleasure,

490
00:45:55,720 --> 00:45:58,600
is joy.

491
00:46:01,400 --> 00:46:05,000
Love then is enjoyment.

492
00:46:05,000 --> 00:46:07,320
It is joy.

493
00:46:07,320 --> 00:46:15,160
Pleasure has always a motive, joy has none, it is timeless.

494
00:46:15,160 --> 00:46:17,880
You can't say, I am joyous.

495
00:46:17,880 --> 00:46:21,960
The moment you have said it, it is gone.

496
00:46:21,960 --> 00:46:29,720
Or if you seek the cause of that joy,

497
00:46:29,720 --> 00:46:36,120
you want it repeated and therefore no longer joy.

498
00:46:36,120 --> 00:46:40,920
So these three things are sexual.

499
00:46:40,920 --> 00:46:44,920
The intelligence of the body,

500
00:46:46,760 --> 00:46:50,440
the capacity, the fullness of love

501
00:46:50,440 --> 00:46:55,400
without the distortions of pleasure,

502
00:46:55,400 --> 00:46:59,720
which doesn't mean that they are not pleasure,

503
00:46:59,720 --> 00:47:04,280
but which doesn't distort the mind.

504
00:47:05,160 --> 00:47:07,640
Look,

505
00:47:09,640 --> 00:47:15,000
you know, most of us have pain, physical pain,

506
00:47:16,120 --> 00:47:19,720
in some form or another.

507
00:47:20,520 --> 00:47:27,000
And that pain generally distorts the mind,

508
00:47:28,840 --> 00:47:31,480
doesn't it?

509
00:47:32,360 --> 00:47:35,240
I wish I hadn't it, I wish I were better,

510
00:47:35,240 --> 00:47:40,920
you know, spent years, days thinking about it.

511
00:47:42,840 --> 00:47:49,000
So when the body has pain, to watch it, to observe it.

512
00:47:50,440 --> 00:47:57,080
And not let it interfere with the mind.

513
00:47:58,040 --> 00:48:01,080
You are following all this?

514
00:48:01,080 --> 00:48:04,200
Do it, sirs.

515
00:48:07,400 --> 00:48:15,960
So the body, the mind including the brain,

516
00:48:16,520 --> 00:48:20,360
and the heart, which is supposed to be love,

517
00:48:20,360 --> 00:48:25,000
all that must be in total harmony.

518
00:48:33,000 --> 00:48:39,640
Now, what is the point of all this?

519
00:48:39,640 --> 00:48:52,040
What is the point of this kind of life,

520
00:48:52,040 --> 00:48:56,120
this kind of harmony?

521
00:48:56,120 --> 00:49:01,240
What good is it in this world,

522
00:49:01,240 --> 00:49:03,240
where everybody is suffering

523
00:49:03,240 --> 00:49:07,560
and one or two people have this ecstatic life?

524
00:49:08,520 --> 00:49:11,800
What is the point of it?

525
00:49:12,520 --> 00:49:16,600
I wonder who is asking this question.

526
00:49:20,440 --> 00:49:23,640
If you are asking this question, what is the point of it,

527
00:49:23,640 --> 00:49:27,480
it has none whatsoever.

528
00:49:30,840 --> 00:49:36,760
But if you have this extraordinary thing going in your life,

529
00:49:36,840 --> 00:49:41,960
then it is everything.

530
00:49:41,960 --> 00:49:48,600
Then you become the teacher, the disciple, the neighbour,

531
00:49:48,600 --> 00:49:55,880
the beauty of the cloud, you are all that.

532
00:49:55,880 --> 00:49:59,000
And that is love.

533
00:49:59,720 --> 00:50:02,360
Then comes another point in meditation.

534
00:50:02,360 --> 00:50:05,800
Do you want to go into all this?

535
00:50:06,760 --> 00:50:09,480
Mark.

536
00:50:12,680 --> 00:50:19,400
You know, the waking mind,

537
00:50:19,400 --> 00:50:23,480
the mind that is awake during the day,

538
00:50:23,480 --> 00:50:31,720
functioning along the lines in which it has been trained,

539
00:50:31,800 --> 00:50:35,800
and the conscious mind,

540
00:50:35,800 --> 00:50:40,760
with all its daily activities,

541
00:50:41,000 --> 00:50:48,440
continues during sleep the same activities.

542
00:50:49,880 --> 00:50:52,920
Have you noticed it?

543
00:50:53,720 --> 00:50:57,160
In most of the dreams there is action going on,

544
00:50:57,160 --> 00:51:00,360
some kind or other, some happening,

545
00:51:00,360 --> 00:51:05,080
which is the same as in daily living.

546
00:51:05,320 --> 00:51:07,960
Right?

547
00:51:07,960 --> 00:51:14,520
So your sleep is a continuation of the waking hours.

548
00:51:15,400 --> 00:51:18,120
Are you following all this?

549
00:51:18,120 --> 00:51:22,280
Are you getting tired at the end of the talk?

550
00:51:24,760 --> 00:51:28,920
I am surprised you are not tired.

551
00:51:29,080 --> 00:51:33,160
You must have had a hard day.

552
00:51:35,320 --> 00:51:39,160
And this is not an entertainment,

553
00:51:39,160 --> 00:51:42,600
this is real work,

554
00:51:42,600 --> 00:51:47,480
work that you have never done before,

555
00:51:47,480 --> 00:51:51,320
therefore it must be exhausting.

556
00:51:51,320 --> 00:51:58,920
So sleep is a continuation of the waking hours.

557
00:51:58,920 --> 00:52:08,920
And we give a lot of mysterious hocus-pocus to dreams.

558
00:52:10,920 --> 00:52:15,960
And then these dreams need to be interpreted,

559
00:52:15,960 --> 00:52:19,960
and you have all the professionals interpreting the dreams.

560
00:52:20,440 --> 00:52:23,240
Which you yourself can observe very simply

561
00:52:23,240 --> 00:52:29,000
if you watch your own life during the daytime.

562
00:52:29,400 --> 00:52:37,320
So the question is, why should there be dreams at all?

563
00:52:37,320 --> 00:52:42,040
Though the psychologists say, from what they have told us,

564
00:52:42,040 --> 00:52:47,640
that you must have dreams, otherwise you will go insane.

565
00:52:47,640 --> 00:52:56,120
But when you have observed very closely your waking hours

566
00:52:56,120 --> 00:53:00,200
and all the activities, the self-centred, the fearful,

567
00:53:00,200 --> 00:53:05,400
the anxious, the guilty, you know, watching it,

568
00:53:05,400 --> 00:53:09,400
attentive all day,

569
00:53:09,400 --> 00:53:14,600
then you will see that when you go to sleep,

570
00:53:15,560 --> 00:53:19,560
that when you go to sleep, you sleep,

571
00:53:19,560 --> 00:53:22,840
you have no dreams,

572
00:53:22,840 --> 00:53:29,560
because during the day you have watched every movement of thought.

573
00:53:29,560 --> 00:53:40,120
The mind has been watching, attentive to every word.

574
00:53:40,120 --> 00:53:43,880
You work it out, you will see the beauty of it,

575
00:53:44,040 --> 00:53:51,000
not the tires, not the boredom of watching,

576
00:53:51,000 --> 00:53:54,280
but the beauty of watching.

577
00:53:54,280 --> 00:54:07,400
So, when the mind is attentive during the day,

578
00:54:07,400 --> 00:54:12,440
then there is attention in sleep.

579
00:54:13,880 --> 00:54:18,120
I am afraid this...

580
00:54:18,120 --> 00:54:23,320
it doesn't matter whether you understand or not, I'll go on.

581
00:54:23,960 --> 00:54:28,600
Because somebody, some day, will understand this.

582
00:54:28,600 --> 00:54:30,760
And it is important to understand it,

583
00:54:30,760 --> 00:54:40,040
because, you see, conscious mind,

584
00:54:40,040 --> 00:54:43,240
the mind that is daily attentive, watching itself,

585
00:54:43,320 --> 00:54:49,320
cannot possibly touch something entirely different.

586
00:54:49,880 --> 00:54:55,800
Though in sleep it is attentive.

587
00:54:57,000 --> 00:55:00,920
And that's why meditation,

588
00:55:00,920 --> 00:55:05,480
the thing that we have talked about during this hour,

589
00:55:05,480 --> 00:55:13,080
becomes extraordinarily important and worthwhile

590
00:55:13,080 --> 00:55:17,720
and full of dignity, grace and beauty,

591
00:55:17,720 --> 00:55:21,560
when you understand attention,

592
00:55:21,560 --> 00:55:28,840
not only during waking hours but also during sleep.

593
00:55:31,080 --> 00:55:37,400
Then the whole of the mind is totally awake.

594
00:55:37,400 --> 00:55:44,120
And beyond that,

595
00:55:45,000 --> 00:55:50,360
every form of description is not the described,

596
00:55:50,360 --> 00:55:55,400
therefore don't talk about it.

597
00:55:58,600 --> 00:56:03,560
All that one can do is point to the door.

598
00:56:03,560 --> 00:56:08,760
And if you are willing to go, take a journey to that door,

599
00:56:08,760 --> 00:56:11,720
it is for you to walk.

600
00:56:11,720 --> 00:56:20,040
Beyond that, nobody can describe the thing that is not nameable.

601
00:56:20,280 --> 00:56:28,280
Whether that nameable is nothing, or everything, doesn't matter.

602
00:56:28,280 --> 00:56:34,600
Anybody who describes it doesn't know.

603
00:56:34,600 --> 00:56:40,840
And one who says he knows, does not know.

604
00:56:58,280 --> 00:57:02,560
Satsang with Mooji
